      { kind: "text", text: "Pregnancy is no longer possible after the uterus is removed. If the ovaries are preserved, they may continue producing hormones until natural menopause. If both ovaries are removed before natural menopause, menopausal symptoms may occur immediately and hormone-related counselling may be needed." }
